    <div class="intro-box">
      <h3>💡 What is this module?</h3>
      <p>The <strong>data</strong> module defines the canonical shapes for every piece of financial data in the system — prices, metrics, trades, news, portfolio positions — plus a fast in-memory cache to avoid redundant API calls.</p>
      <p class="analogy">"Think of it as a <strong>filing cabinet with standardized forms</strong> — every document that enters the system must fit into a pre-defined form (Pydantic model), and the cabinet keeps a copy so you never have to request the same document twice."</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="toc" id="toc"><h2>Table of Contents</h2></nav>

    <h2 id="architecture">Architecture Overview</h2>
    <p>The data module provides two core services: schema definitions (models.py) and a caching layer (cache.py). Models are consumed by both the tools layer for API response parsing and by the agent layer for state management.</p>
    <div class="mermaid-wrapper" onclick="openOverlay(this)">
      <pre class="mermaid" data-source="graph TD
    A[Financial Datasets API] -->|JSON| B[Pydantic Response Models]
    B --> C[Domain Models]
    C --> D[Cache Layer]
    D --> E[Analyst Agents]
    F[Agent State] --> G[AgentStateData / Metadata]
    G --> E
    H[Portfolio Manager] --> I[Portfolio / Position]
    style B fill:#58a6ff,stroke:#333,color:#000
    style D fill:#d29922,stroke:#333,color:#000
    style C fill:#3fb950,stroke:#333,color:#000">graph TD
    A[Financial Datasets API] -->|JSON| B[Pydantic Response Models]
    B --> C[Domain Models]
    C --> D[Cache Layer]
    D --> E[Analyst Agents]
    F[Agent State] --> G[AgentStateData / Metadata]
    G --> E
    H[Portfolio Manager] --> I[Portfolio / Position]
