    style C fill:#3fb950,stroke:#333,color:#000</pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="data-flow">Data Flow &amp; Cache Lifecycle</h2>
    <p>When a tool function fetches data, the response is parsed via a Pydantic response model, then the extracted domain objects are stored in the cache's internal dict. Subsequent requests for the same data return from cache without a network call.</p>
    <div class="mermaid-wrapper" onclick="openOverlay(this)">
      <pre class="mermaid" data-source="sequenceDiagram
    participant Tool as tools.api
    participant Model as data.models
    participant Cache as data.cache
    participant Agent as Analyst Agent
    Tool->>Model: Parse JSON → PriceResponse
    Model-->>Tool: list[Price]
    Tool->>Cache: cache.prices[key] = data
    Agent->>Cache: get_cache().get_prices(key)
    alt Hit
        Cache-->>Agent: list[Price]
    else Miss
        Cache-->>Agent: None
        Agent->>Tool: get_prices(ticker, ...)
    end">sequenceDiagram
    participant Tool as tools.api
    participant Model as data.models
    participant Cache as data.cache
    participant Agent as Analyst Agent
    Tool->>Model: Parse JSON → PriceResponse
    Model-->>Tool: list[Price]
    Tool->>Cache: cache.prices[key] = data
    Agent->>Cache: get_cache().get_prices(key)
    alt Hit
        Cache-->>Agent: list[Price]
    else Miss
        Cache-->>Agent: None
        Agent->>Tool: get_prices(ticker, ...)
    end</pre>
    </div>

