        <tr><td>Portfolio manager</td><td>data.models</td><td>Manages <code>Portfolio</code> and <code>Position</code> instances</td></tr>
        <tr><td>graph.state</td><td>data.models</td><td>References <code>AgentStateData</code> and <code>AgentStateMetadata</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>cli / API</td><td>data.cache</td><td>Cache persists across agent runs within a session</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="deep-dive">Deep Dive</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h4>📝 models.py (174 LOC)</h4>
        <p>The schema backbone — 12 domain models, 6 response wrappers, 2 TypedDict state containers. Every field is typed and documented with Pydantic v2.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🗄️ cache.py (71 LOC)</h4>
        <p>Simple but effective in-memory cache. Separate dicts for prices, metrics, line items, insider trades, and news. Dedup via <code>_merge_data()</code> on date/id keys.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>📊 FinancialMetrics</h4>
        <p>The largest model — 44 nullable float fields covering market_cap, pe_ratio, pb_ratio, return_on_equity, net_margin, revenue_growth, and many more fundamentals.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h4>🔄 LineItem Flexibility</h4>
        <p>Uses Pydantic's <code>extra="allow"</code> config to accept arbitrary financial statement fields, making it adaptable to any line item search result.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

